From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Fursund <jens@spectralcompute.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip DOCA's CUDA type declarations when cuda.h is included

doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h declares the CUDA driver types it uses
(CUresult, CUdevice, CUdeviceptr, CUcontext and three enums) for builds
without cuda.h, which NCCL's are (DOCA_VERBS_USE_CUDA_WRAPPER). A
translation unit that has cuda.h before it, directly or through a CUDA
runtime header that also declares the driver API (SCALE's does), gets
each type twice: "multiple definition of 'enum cudaError_enum'" and
eight more errors.

Skip the declarations when cuda.h's include guard, __cuda_cuda_h__, is
defined. The wrapper functions are then declared with cuda.h's types,
which the declarations stand in for. A build without cuda.h is
unchanged.

Checked with g++ and CUDA 12.8's cuda.h: the header after cuda.h had 9
errors and has none, and on its own it compiles as before.
---
 .../doca-gpunetio/src/doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h    |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/transport/net_ib/gdaki/doca-gpunetio/src/doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h b/src/transport/net_ib/gdaki/doca-gpunetio/src/doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h
index d748e1b..b4ae453 100644
--- a/src/transport/net_ib/gdaki/doca-gpunetio/src/doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h
+++ b/src/transport/net_ib/gdaki/doca-gpunetio/src/doca_verbs_cuda_wrapper.h
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ extern "C" {
 #ifdef DOCA_VERBS_USE_CUDA_WRAPPER
 
 /* CUDA type declarations for builds without cuda.h */
+#ifndef __cuda_cuda_h__
 typedef enum cudaError_enum {
     CUDA_SUCCESS = 0,
     CUDA_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED = 3,
@@ -60,6 +61,7 @@ typedef enum CUdevice_attribute_enum {
 } CUdevice_attribute;
 
 typedef void *CUcontext;
+#endif /* __cuda_cuda_h__ */
 
 /* Wrapper function declarations */
 CUresult doca_verbs_wrapper_cuDeviceGetAttribute(int *pi, CUdevice_attribute attrib, CUdevice dev);
